  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Support to UN and Other Multilateral Processes over the Remaining Years of the Ongoing MFF 2021-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under Partnerships&apos; MAAP 2025-2027, the Overall Objective of this action is to cover relevant UN or other multilateral processes (and events/summits) expected between 2025 (Q3-Q4) and 2027 that the EU has a specific interest in supporting financially.The Specific Objectives of this action are the support of: &amp;nbsp;Upcoming multilateral processes in follow-up to the Summit of the Future, in implementation of the Pact for the Future and its commitments and implementation of the 2030 Agenda, and in preparation for the post-2030 framework.Upcoming processes in follow-up to UN and other multilateral high-level events (contributing to the implementation of the 2030 Agenda) and their commitments: e.g., the 5th Conference on Least Developed Countries (LDC5), the 4th Conference on Small Island Developing States (SIDS4), the 69th UN Civil Society Conference (UNCSC69), and the (upcoming) 3rd Conference on Landlocked Developing Countries (LLDC3).&amp;nbsp;Processes of global governance reform in UN and multilateral fora.&amp;nbsp;Partnerships with UN, other multilateral fora, and partners (including civil society at large), with the aim to reinforce EU outreach and bridgebuilding for an effective and inclusive rules-based multilateralism.Concrete measures under this action will be designed in coordination with also other actions under the relevant thematic or geographic MIPs.</narrative>
  </description>
